---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Pilum · Download privacy" description="How Pilum uses your email when you request an alpha download.">
  <main class="section privacy-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="/">← Back to Pilum</a>
      <p class="label">Your email</p>
      <h1>Download privacy</h1>
      <p>When you request the alpha, we save your email address, selected platform, request dates, delivery status and whether you asked for updates. We use your email to send your selected platform’s download link and help with your request.</p>
      <p>Checking “Keep me posted about Pilum” is optional. Downloading does not require signing up for updates. Use the unsubscribe or preferences links in your Pilum email to stop updates or change your choice. Unsubscribing does not affect download emails you request. You can also ask us to stop updates or delete your address by emailing <a href="mailto:info@pilumrts.com">info@pilumrts.com</a>.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare processes the request, stores these records and delivers the email. We also send a signup summary (email address, selected platform, update preference and signup time) to a private Pilum team channel on Discord. The download links expire after seven days. We record when a link is used to confirm the address can receive email. Email security scanners may also open links.</p>
      <p>We use short-lived, salted hashes for request limits instead of storing raw IP addresses in the download database. These expire within an hour. Cloudflare may process connection information to operate and protect its services.</p>
      <p>We do not sell your email address. We keep your download request while it is useful for the alpha and its support; you can request deletion at any time.</p>
      <p class="small">Updated 22 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
